  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Providing safe and decent living conditions for people affected by the escalation of the conflict in the Bereznehuvatska community of Mykolaiv region</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtUnder the proposed project, AoS plans to carry out repairs to the houses of Mykolaiv region damaged as a result of the conflict, which may include roof repairs, installation of windows and/or doors for 49 households in Bereznehuvate, Liubomyryivka, Yakovlivka and Veselyi Kut villages, at a cost of up to USD 4,000 per household. The project aims to provide vulnerable families with decent warm and dry basic functional space, prevent unnecessary displacement and create conditions for the return of displaced families.ltbrgtlt/pgtltpgtCurrently, people in the selected location are returning to their homes, most of which are damaged or totally destroyed. As a result of the project, 49 households will be repaired, where the beneficiaries will be able to live in comfortable conditions, as the community is currently in great need of construction materials and the reconstruction of affected households and social institutions. The actual completion of the activity is not the completion of the repair work, but the actual return of the beneficiary&apos;s family to the repaired house, as the ultimate goal is not to repair the house, but to provide assistance to the family. The main categories of beneficiaries to be covered under the proposed activity include: internally displaced persons, persons affected by the military conflict, persons with limited mobility and disabilities, single elderly persons, etc.ltbrgtlt/pgtltpgtThe assessment work will be carried out by the team of the Charity Organization &quot;Charitable Foundation &quot;Angels of Salvation&quot;, and the purchase of materials for repairs according to the created estimate and direct repair of selected households will be carried out by the builders of the subcontractor&apos;s company, which will be determined by tender selection.ltbrgtlt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
